between mocks, stubs, fakes, and other terms used to identify and/or
categorize types or services used in testing that are not suitable for
production but are necessary for the unit test. These dependencies may
have functionality that is different, missing, and/or the same as
their real counterparts.
For example, the TestUserInterface class could be referred to as a
